{"id": "EUVD-2026-80255", "enisaUuid": "d4254fe4-3e4b-3dd3-89c1-ce5af76f05af", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: SCO: hold sk properly in sco_conn_ready\n\nsk deref in sco_conn_ready must be done either under conn->lock, or\nholding a refcount, to avoid concurrent close. conn->sk and parent sk is\ncurrently accessed without either, and without checking parent->sk_state:\n\n    [Task 1]            [Task 2]\n                        sco_sock_release\n    sco_conn_ready\n      sk = conn->sk\n                          lock_sock(sk)\n                            conn->sk = NULL\n      lock_sock(sk)\n                          release_sock(sk)\n                          sco_sock_kill(sk)\n       UAF on sk deref\n\nand similarly for access to sco_get_sock_listen() return value.\n\nFix possible UAF by holding sk refcount in sco_conn_ready() and making\nsco_get_sock_listen() increase refcount. Also recheck after lock_sock\nthat the socket is still valid.  Adjust conn->sk locking so it's\nprotected also by lock_sock() of the associated socket if any.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T08:24:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T14:38:26", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50aae396dc30377bec8e3b181b8346f8fd38f7d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e3840578aaad1a296aab1eaaa89ea3b7d5cbae1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d141d9b769bcd1b747898528c5023270cda040f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73cb063f5ec6ca51eb1e246c6d332563002ac277", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7199c78c3a3e399a4dc439d845826793880ccedc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e37f6452d586b95c346a9abdd2fb80b67794f39"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g3p6-8r9x-w9g7", "CVE-2026-89774"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19c7157a-49c6-3de5-a4cb-8d0c8692c9e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "1ebadf8b-ca36-3ca7-bf6e-f120b8649827", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <7199c78c3a3e399a4dc439d845826793880ccedc"}, {"id": "2d297f77-94f6-3484-a258-502f92242c76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <73cb063f5ec6ca51eb1e246c6d332563002ac277"}, {"id": "47a9c6f1-4741-378f-96d6-fa0a3ac2c48a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "612be5d1-07a4-3af2-a9b3-5c31383462b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <50aae396dc30377bec8e3b181b8346f8fd38f7d8"}, {"id": "76ffe281-afa7-3fa7-ac4c-9efb8b4611e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "7b6a5975-18ea-3dbc-a492-f9caf6a8f8c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "86238a4e-41f6-3e24-aaf1-e0b0ab23f080", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "8bf2d736-d1d4-38f9-b11f-a37108be89de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "8e1e8432-88d1-3423-bb77-1245616f357a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "a0a52145-9e51-335d-9fa0-658fb64dc043", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c24fda62b601d6f9ca5e992502578c4310876f <d141d9b769bcd1b747898528c5023270cda040f2"}, {"id": "c3bcbe3e-bca4-3140-9f85-0e3596c46262", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "d221ca95-028a-30b4-a31d-2d855c38389e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27c2